From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 07:15:00 +0200
Subject: fix: hide Impersonate User masthead action when Group model is
 unavailable

The masthead's "Impersonate User" action unconditionally opens a modal that
watches user.openshift.io/v1 Group to populate the group picker. On a
cluster that doesn't run OpenShift's user/OAuth API server aggregation (e.g.
this repo's VictoriaMetrics-based cluster), that API doesn't exist, so the
modal always shows "Failed to load groups" / "Model does not exist" and the
feature is unusable.

Gate the masthead action on the Group model actually being present in
cluster API discovery (via useK8sModel, the same mechanism used elsewhere
in console core to detect optional CRDs/aggregated APIs), so the item is
hidden entirely on clusters without it instead of showing a broken modal.

Note: useK8sModel must be imported from @console/shared/src/hooks/useK8sModel
(the internal re-export also used by user-provider.ts), not from the
@console/dynamic-plugin-sdk package root - it isn't re-exported there.

